{"text":"Metformin remains first-line therapy for type 2 diabetes mellitus, but long-term use can lower vitamin B12 and cause peripheral neuropathy. In our cohort, patients who ate oily fish and drank green tea had lower HbA1c; those on warfarin were told to avoid grapefruit juice. BRCA1 carriers were excluded.","recorded":"2026-11-19","response":{"ok":true,"model":"claude-opus-5-5","mode":"live","selector":"claude-opus-5-5","entities":[{"id":"e1","text":"Metformin","start":0,"end":9,"type":"chemical","ontology":"chebi","matches":[{"id":"CHEBI:747603","label":"metformin(2+)","score":0.032266458495966696,"retrievers":{"bm25":1,"dense-qwen3":3},"url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:747603"},{"id":"CHEBI:6801","label":"metformin","score":0.03225806451612903,"retrievers":{"bm25":2,"dense-qwen3":2},"url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:6801"},{"id":"CHEBI:6802","label":"metformin hydrochloride","score":0.030776515151515152,"retrievers":{"bm25":6,"dense-qwen3":4},"url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:6802"},{"id":"CHEBI:90688","label":"metformin(1+)","score":0.030330882352941176,"retrievers":{"bm25":4,"dense-qwen3":8},"url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:90688"},{"id":"CHEBI:753289","label":"metformin glycinate","score":0.030309988518943745,"retrievers":{"bm25":5,"dense-qwen3":7},"url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:753289"}],"notes":[],"pick":{"selector":"claude-opus-5-5","status":"match","id":"CHEBI:6801","label":"metformin","url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:6801","confidence":0.95,"explanation":"The unqualified mention 'Metformin' in a clinical drug context refers to the parent compound metformin, not to its salt or ionic forms."},"more":[{"id":"CHEBI:90875","label":"Synjardy","score":0.029206349206349208,"retrievers":{"bm25":3,"dense-qwen3":15},"url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:90875"},{"id":"CHEBI:3